  "leanSource": "import Lean\nimport Obsmetrologia\nopen Lean Elab Command\n\n/-!\nIdentification-key census.\n\nAn identification is *spent* where `Quot.sound` or `Quotient.sound` is applied.\nA house spend (inside an `Obsmetrologia.` constant) is keyed by the relation or\nsetoid it identifies along: the head constant of the `r` argument of\n`Quot.sound` or the `s` argument of `Quotient.sound`. A spend made inside a\nLean-core constant is keyed `core:<constant>` — so `funext`, which core proves by\n`Quot.sound`, is one key. A theorem inherits every key in the transitive closure\nof the constants it uses, core and house alike. The number of distinct keys a\ntheorem inherits is the number of independent identifications it rests on.\n\nReading through an identification (`Quot.mk`, `Quot.lift`, `Quotient.lift`,\n`Quot.ind`) spends nothing and is not a key.\n\nOutput, tab-separated:\n  `#theorems\\t<n>`\n  `#keys\\t<n>`\n  `#key\\t<key>\\t<theorems inheriting it>`   (one per key, most inherited first)\n  `#hist\\t<distinct keys>\\t<theorems>`       (one per bucket)\n  `<theorem>\\t<distinct keys>\\t<comma-joined keys>`   (one per house theorem)\n-/\n\ndef isHouse (n : Name) : Bool := n.toString.startsWith \"Obsmetrologia.\"\n\n/-- The string-valued dot components of a name, ignoring anonymous and numeric\nsegments (`Obsmetrologia.Foo.bar` -> `[\"Obsmetrologia\", \"Foo\", \"bar\"]`). -/\npartial def nameStrComponents : Name → List String\n  | .anonymous => []\n  | .str p s => nameStrComponents p ++ [s]\n  | .num p _ => nameStrComponents p\n\n/-- Lean-elaborator-generated declaration names -- recursors, injectivity/\nno-confusion lemmas, equation-compiler helpers, sizeOf plumbing, well-founded\nmatch/proof helpers, etc. -- that must never be counted as house theorems.\nTrue when any dot-separated component begins with `_` (`_proof_1`, `_eq_1`,\n`_unfold`, ...), or the last component is one of the fixed auto-generated\nnames, or begins with `match_`/`proof_`, or is `eq_` followed by one or more\ndigits (`eq_1`, `eq_2`, ...). A `mk.sizeOf_spec`/`mk.injEq`/`mk.inj`/\n`mk.noConfusion` name is already caught by the last-component rule, since\n`sizeOf_spec`/`injEq`/`inj`/`noConfusion` is its own last component. See\nAGENTS.md defect note (2026-09-21): every census program in this directory\nhad been counting these as house theorems, inflating every \"theorems\" total\nand (worst, in the certificate-shape census) dominating the top lists with\n`Algebra.*.mk.sizeOf_spec` entries. -/\ndef isAutoGenerated (n : Name) : Bool :=\n  let cs := nameStrComponents n\n  if cs.any (·.startsWith \"_\") then true\n  else\n    match cs.getLast? with\n    | none => false\n    | some last =>\n      [\n        \"sizeOf_spec\", \"injEq\", \"inj\", \"noConfusion\", \"noConfusionType\",\n        \"casesOn\", \"recOn\", \"rec\", \"brecOn\", \"binductionOn\",\n        \"below\", \"ibelow\", \"toCtorIdx\", \"ofNat_toCtorIdx\", \"ctorIdx\", \"ctorElim\"\n      ].contains last\n      || last.startsWith \"match_\"\n      || last.startsWith \"proof_\"\n      || (last.startsWith \"eq_\" && last.length > 3 && (last.drop 3).all Char.isDigit)\n\ndef isSpend (c : Name) : Bool := c == ``Quot.sound || c == ``Quotient.sound\n\n/-- The keys of every maximal `Quot.sound`/`Quotient.sound` application in an\nexpression: the head constant of the relation/setoid argument, or an anonymous\nmarker naming the owning constant when that argument is not headed by a constant. -/\npartial def spendKeysOfExpr (owner : Name) (e : Expr) (acc : Array String) : Array String :=\n  match e with\n  | .app .. =>\n    let fn := e.getAppFn\n    let args := e.getAppArgs\n    let acc := match fn with\n      | .const c _ =>\n        if isSpend c then\n          if h : 1 < args.size then\n            match args[1].getAppFn with\n            | .const rc _ => acc.push rc.toString\n            | _ => acc.push s!\"<anon:{owner}>\"\n          else acc.push s!\"<partial:{owner}>\"\n        else acc\n      | _ => acc\n    let acc := match fn with\n      | .const _ _ => acc\n      | _ => spendKeysOfExpr owner fn acc\n    args.foldl (fun acc a => spendKeysOfExpr owner a acc) acc\n  | .lam _ t b _ => spendKeysOfExpr owner b (spendKeysOfExpr owner t acc)\n  | .forallE _ t b _ => spendKeysOfExpr owner b (spendKeysOfExpr owner t acc)\n  | .letE _ t v b _ => spendKeysOfExpr owner b (spendKeysOfExpr owner v (spendKeysOfExpr owner t acc))\n  | .mdata _ b => spendKeysOfExpr owner b acc\n  | .proj _ _ b => spendKeysOfExpr owner b acc\n  | _ => acc\n\n/-- The keys a constant inherits: its own spends (keyed by relation if house,\nby constant if core) plus every key of every constant it uses, memoized. -/\npartial def keysOf (env : Environment) (cache : IO.Ref (Std.HashMap Name (Array String)))\n    (n : Name) : IO (Array String) := do\n  if let some s := (← cache.get).get? n then return s\n  cache.modify (·.insert n #[])  -- cycle guard\n  let some ci := env.find? n | return #[]\n  let used := ci.getUsedConstantsAsSet\n  let mut acc : Array String := #[]\n  if used.toList.any isSpend then\n    if isHouse n then\n      let ks := match ci with\n        | .thmInfo t => spendKeysOfExpr n t.value #[]\n        | .defnInfo d => spendKeysOfExpr n d.value #[]\n        | _ => #[]\n      let ks := if ks.isEmpty then #[s!\"<unkeyed:{n}>\"] else ks\n      for k in ks do if !acc.contains k then acc := acc.push k\n    else\n      acc := acc.push s!\"core:{n}\"\n  for u in used.toList do\n    if isSpend u then continue\n    for k in (← keysOf env cache u) do\n      if !acc.contains k then acc := acc.push k\n  cache.modify (·.insert n acc)\n  return acc\n\n#eval show CommandElabM Unit from do\n  let env ← getEnv\n  let cache ← IO.mkRef ({} : Std.HashMap Name (Array String))\n  let mut keyCount : Std.HashMap String Nat := {}\n  let mut hist : Std.HashMap Nat Nat := {}\n  let mut rows : Array String := #[]\n  let mut excluded := 0\n  for (n, ci) in env.constants.toList do\n    if isHouse n && !n.isInternal then\n      if let .thmInfo _ := ci then\n        if isAutoGenerated n then\n          excluded := excluded + 1\n        else\n          let ks ← keysOf env cache n\n          hist := hist.insert ks.size ((hist.getD ks.size 0) + 1)\n          for k in ks do keyCount := keyCount.insert k ((keyCount.getD k 0) + 1)\n          rows := rows.push s!\"{n}\\t{ks.size}\\t{String.intercalate \",\" ks.toList}\"\n  IO.println s!\"#excluded-auto-generated\\t{excluded}\"\n  IO.println s!\"#theorems\\t{rows.size}\"\n  IO.println s!\"#keys\\t{keyCount.size}\"\n  for (k, c) in (keyCount.toArray.qsort (fun a b => a.2 > b.2 || (a.2 == b.2 && a.1 < b.1))) do\n    IO.println s!\"#key\\t{k}\\t{c}\"\n  for (k, c) in (hist.toArray.qsort (fun a b => a.1 < b.1)) do\n    IO.println s!\"#hist\\t{k}\\t{c}\"\n  for r in rows.qsort (· < ·) do IO.println r\n",
  "reading": "An identification is spent where Quot.sound or Quotient.sound is applied. A house spend is keyed by the relation or setoid it identifies along; a spend made inside a Lean-core constant (funext above all: core proves function extensionality by Quot.sound) is keyed core:<constant>. A theorem inherits every key in its full dependency closure, core and house alike; the number of distinct keys it inherits is the number of independent identifications it rests on. Owner-ruled 2026-09-03: the library is meant to spend exactly one identification, at the articulating root, with everything downstream inheriting it — a theorem whose only key is the root is settled, any other key is postulated. Reading through an identification (Quot.mk, Quot.lift, Quotient.lift) spends nothing and is not a key; the identification-site census counts those uses and so over-prices, while missing every spend made inside core.",
